== putting values in ==
  hello, Matt
  3 apples and 4 pears is 7 fruit
  in capitals: MATT
  the longer word: Profi-C
  a set looks like {1, 2, 3}
  and a hole is written {{ like this }}
== saying how ==
  plain:      1234.5
  to a penny: 1234.50
  with commas:1,234.50
  the date:   2026-08-15
  the time:   14:30
  through Format: 1234.50
  rounded to 2:   1234.5
== a block, as written ==
Usage: pc run <file>

A path may hold \ and " and {{ freely,
because nothing in here is read as anything.
  one line, no escapes: C:\Users\Matt
== quotes inside a block ==
She said "no" twice
a block is opened with """ or more
and the last word is "this"
== apart and back together ==
  words:      4
  hyphenated: the-quick-brown-fox
  shouted:    THE QUICK BROWN FOX
  quietly:    the quick brown fox
  as a title: The quick brown fox
  swapped:    the slow brown fox
  counts:     1, 2, 3
== by position ==
  first:      c
  last:       t
  spelled:    c a s t
== text into numbers ==
  an integer: 42
  a real:     3.5
  a boolean:  true
  a ratio:    22|7
  written /:  22|7
  a whole:    5|1
  not a number: false
